<article class="env-definition" id="01C2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01C2">Definition <span data-tag="01C2">17.13.1</span>.</a> A <em>closed immersion of ringed spaces</em><a class="footnotemark" href="#a0000423398" id="a0000423398-mark"><sup>1</sup></a> is a morphism $i : (Z, \mathcal{O}_ Z) \to (X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$ with the following properties: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The map $i$ is a closed immersion of topological spaces. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The associated map $\mathcal{O}_ X \to i_*\mathcal{O}_ Z$ is surjective. Denote the kernel by $\mathcal{I}$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module $\mathcal{I}$ is locally generated by sections. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>